{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/459787-valkyrie-versatility","id":459787,"title":"Valkyrie versatility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-28T02:58:29-07:00","id":459787,"title":"Valkyrie versatility","content":"I was looking through Compacts and Conspiracies and noticed how versatile task force valkyrie is- a joint task force that might include any US government agencies and representatives of any NATO country's governmental agencies too.<br /> <br /> So in a valkyrie game, you could have anything from marines taking out a zombie outbreak in the middle east, to an IRS team looking for vampires who use creative accounting, to CDC agents trying to stop a lycanthropic STD outbreak, to secret service agents who look for witches who make their own money. <br /> <br /> Has anyone taken advantage of that versatility when coming up with valkyrie character ideas as a player, or coming up with a more off the wall idea for a valkyrie game as a storyteller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T08:22:03-07:00","id":460023,"title":"","content":"At a basic(very basic) level, I've used military backgrounds for just about every single TFV character I've played. Dunno, guess it's just what I've always felt comfortable with. But I agree. TFV is very open when it comes to who it's members can be and what they might be facing off against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:22:34-07:00","id":460523,"title":"","content":"Well that makes sense, when it comes to monster fighting, a military style attack is undoubtedly the first thing that comes to mine, especially with the nature of valkyrie endowments.<br /> <br /> One doesn't generally think of an IRS agent or a CDC doctor needing superweapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T19:21:26-07:00","id":460603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/459787-valkyrie-versatility?p=460523#post460523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One doesn't generally think of an IRS agent or a CDC doctor needing superweapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they have nailed a few people to wall about tax evasion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T03:41:43-07:00","id":462070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/459787-valkyrie-versatility?p=460523#post460523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that makes sense, when it comes to monster fighting, a military style attack is undoubtedly the first thing that comes to mine, especially with the nature of valkyrie endowments.<br /> <br /> One doesn't generally think of an IRS agent or a CDC doctor needing superweapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about the IRS agent, but the CDC doctor in WoD? Hack, they might not fight at the front lines, but they would be absolutely perfect for finding monster outbreaks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:10:31-07:00","id":462390,"title":"","content":"Considering that there are diseases that <i>fight back</i> in the NWoD, you might want to have a good sidearm when you go in and treat the contagious case of chicken-pox that also creates a cannibalistic hive-mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:10:41-07:00","id":462731,"title":"","content":"... That is an awesome character concept. Wasn't there a Manga sort of like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:21:23-07:00","id":462743,"title":"","content":"I'm... not sure? I mostly picked alliterative words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:39:56-07:00","id":463009,"title":"","content":"I think the Trauma Center games for the Nintendo wii and DS might be what SoulGambit is thinking of. They are done in an anime/manga style and using hyper tech and mysterious powers to fight super diseases beyond the understanding of modern medicine (created by crazy death cults at that) forms the basis of the plot of the first two games and the pre-sequal that takes place between them. Considering that the last game in the series also involves a ghost leading one of the playable doctors to the source of the psychosis inducing viral hemorrhagic fever tearing up Portland and a playable medical examiner who is basically a Sin-eater of the stricken AND forgotten threshold, I'd say that the series would be perfect inspiration for a CDC Valkyrie campaign, if you assume that the taskforce's CDC members are less hostile to supernaturals that are trying to help. But my personal head canon is that Valkerie is just as interested in using friendly supernaturals to protect American/NATO interests as it is in protecting those interests from the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:11:10-07:00","id":463197,"title":"","content":"That does sound like a great premise for a valkyrie game. <br /> <br /> As for your headcanon, considering the US might have Project Twilight out to weaponize the supernatural, and company zero, which either assigns supernatural soldiers for missions or collects magic items for the US government, it wouldn't be hard to picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}